  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "D-D thermonuclear fusion (~10⁸ K / ~10 keV) is achievable via acoustic cavitation, closing the ~4 orders-of-magnitude temperature gap above demonstrated sonoluminescence conditions (7,000–16,000 K)",
      "Fusion gain Q ≥ ~3.5 at baseline parameters is reachable, with commercial viability targeting Q ≈ 10 or higher",
      "Acoustic driver wall-plug efficiency (η_driver) near 85% is attainable, far beyond the only measured datapoint of Kp ≥ 55% (planar coupling coefficient)",
      "Acoustic driver power can scale to ~100 MW per module — roughly 6,250× the largest demonstrated commercial ultrasonic unit (Hielscher UIP16000 at 16 kW)",
      "Fusion energy thermalizes in the D₂O medium and is recoverable via a conventional Rankine/sCO₂ thermal cycle at ~35% efficiency",
      "PZT piezoelectric transducers can survive neutron irradiation from D-D fusion (2.45 MeV neutrons at commercial flux) with acceptable lifetime",
      "A deuterated liquid vessel (~3 m radius, ~113 m³ D₂O per module) can sustain coherent cavitation and confine the required fusion power density"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "Plasma confinement coils / HTS magnets and cryoplant (CAS 220103 → $0)",
      "Tritium breeding blanket (CAS 220106 eliminated — D-D fuel cycle)",
      "RF / NBI auxiliary heating systems (CAS 220104 → $0)",
      "Direct energy conversion hardware (CAS 220109 → $0; thermal cycle used instead)",
      "External tritium supply infrastructure (D-D produces tritium as byproduct rather than requiring breeding)"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Acoustic transducer array (CAS 220107-equivalent) — piezoelectric driver replacing coils + heating subsystems",
      "Large D₂O vessel fill (~113 m³/module at $300–$475/kg, ~$56M fill + ~$15M structure per module)",
      "D₂O circulation and management systems (override accounts C220106, C220108)",
      "Tritium byproduct containment/separation for D-D-produced tritium (~50% of reactions)",
      "Neutron-irradiation-qualified PZT transducer replacement program (transducer replacement amortized at ~$6.2M/yr)"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Foundational scientific viability: ~4 orders-of-magnitude temperature gap from demonstrated sonoluminescence (~16,000 K) to D-D fusion (~10⁸ K) with no published theoretical mechanism to bridge it; Taleyarkhan (2002) fusion claims discredited and found to be research misconduct (2008)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "No reactor design, shielding concept, or energy conversion pathway has been published; entire CAS10-LCOE capital structure rests on speculative placeholders",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Acoustic driver wall-plug efficiency assumed at 85% is unsupported — only Kp ≥ 55% (planar coupling coefficient, not wall-plug) is measured; at η_driver = 0.55, breakeven Q rises from ~3.5 to ~5.2",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Acoustic driver power scale-up from 64 kW (largest demonstrated cluster) to 100 MW/module is ~1,560× unconstrained, with unsolved engineering limits on cavity volume, transducer packing, cavitation threshold, and acoustic interference",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Q and acoustic power are physically coupled unknowns — sensitivity sweeps that hold Q=10 fixed across power levels misrepresent the joint design-space risk",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "D₂O supply chain concentration — India and Canada account for ~80% of global D₂O exports by value (2023 UN Comtrade), creating geopolitical supply risk at commercial deployment scale",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "D-D neutron flux (2.45 MeV, ~50% of reactions) requires substantial shielding and activation management; PZT transducer lifetime under neutron irradiation is completely unstudied",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Scientific reputational overhang from Taleyarkhan misconduct case has made sonofusion a research-funding pariah, suppressing theoretical and experimental follow-up that could narrow the temperature gap",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Company disclosure is minimal — no reactor design, energy conversion specification, performance targets, funding details, or development timeline published by Sonofusion Energy",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Regulatory pathway for a novel acoustic fusion concept is undefined; NRC fusion framework may require special review",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
